  "records": {
    "description": "Multiplies two unsigned 8/16/32-bit numbers to produce an unsigned product using a radix-4 Booth algorithm and specific CSA/CCA looping approaches.",
    "input": "Two unsigned 8 / 16 / 32 bit numbers",
    "output": "Unsigned 16 / 32 / 64 bit product",
    "speed": "Processes two bits of A every 3rd, so does 4 / 8 / 16 iterations with one iteration being 3rd. The 32 bit multiplier shows the result less than 10 seconds after pressing the \"Start\" button (as far as I am aware).",
    "considerations": [
      "Uses 3t looping CSA shown in Bennyscube video and 3t CCA by Amino.",
      "Uses the Radix-4 Booth algorithm which essentially also works for signed numbers in twos complement, but this would require additional logic afaik"
    ]
  },
